        <body>
            <div xml:id="d767">

                <pb facs="0731" n="615" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg615"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 815.51/337.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic"> Wm. C. Sheldon and Company, Bankers, to the Secretary
                        of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-05-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 15, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My dear Mr. Secretary: It gives me great pleasure to introduce herewith Mr. Sol
                    Wexler, Vice President of the Whitney-Central National Bank of New Orleans, who
                    is associated with us in the loan to Honduras. The Whitney-Central National Bank
                    is proposing to advance to Honduras $500,000, and Mr. Wexler is anxious to
                    submit the papers to you.</p>
                <p>Thanking you for any courtesies you may extend to Mr. Wexler, I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">George R. Sheldon.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Note.</hi>—Mr. Wexler called at the Department
                        on May 17 and spoke with Mr. Doyle and Mr. Wright.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
